# Baseline/path allowlist for tools/check-headless-launch.py's rules 3 (an
# unsuppressed console-program spawn) and 4 (the same, declared in JSON/YAML).
#
# One "relative/path.ext:line  reason" entry per line (whitespace-separated;
# the reason is free text, required only for a human reviewer's benefit --
# the checker itself just matches the "path:line" token). Blank lines and
# lines starting with "#" are ignored.
#
# Rule 4 (JSON) has no inline-comment escape hatch (JSON has no comment
# syntax), so this file is its only option there; a YAML file may instead
# carry an inline "# headless-guard: allow <why>" comment. Rule 3 (Python)
# normally uses that same inline-comment escape hatch too -- this file's
# entries below are a ONE-TIME BASELINE seeded when the rule first shipped
# (ThomasMichon/copilot-extensions#789), not meant to accumulate further:
# triage each one (ThomasMichon/copilot-extensions#5518) into either a real
# fix (remove the entry) or a reviewed, specific inline comment (remove the
# entry here, add the comment at the call site instead). Do not add a new
# baseline-style entry here for freshly-written code -- use the inline
# comment for that.
